{"commit": "aed424a778f43373824232e242e4f7894ba221f1", "id": "aed424a778f43373824232e242e4f7894ba221f1-1", "language": "rust", "reason": "Selected test is not present at the fixed revision: src/ext_slice.rs - ext_slice::ByteSlice::splitn_str (line 1309)", "repo": "https://github.com/BurntSushi/bstr", "reproduction": {"attempt": "20260923T224217Z-59d9bbe1", "evidence_sha256": {"evidence/aed424a778f43373824232e242e4f7894ba221f1-1/20260923T224217Z-59d9bbe1/origin.json": "8f95f4f5ac5b1d3ebed99e5528215e73a04b994c256dabb4e967912ca187e364", "evidence/aed424a778f43373824232e242e4f7894ba221f1-1/20260923T224217Z-59d9bbe1/proposal.json": "261369e438ddfff97b3f27bf435273d206072436d247162c5428a88e6fa01c35"}, "provenance": "verbatim"}, "shard": "bstr", "status": "blocked", "subject": "api: fix splitn_str and rsplitn_str", "summary": "`SplitN::next` short-circuited on `count == limit` without checking whether the underlying split had already produced its final chunk, so `splitn_str(n, needle)` emitted a spurious trailing empty slice whenever the haystack contained fewer than `n-1` needle occurrences. The fix gates the early return on `self.split.done` as well.", "updated_at": "2026-09-23T22:42:17.291120+00:00"}
